Why the DUT's log is the subject, and not a convenience.  The TFS opens its "Logging
specifications" section by saying: "There are no explicit logging requirements for this
project. However, to help with debugging customer issues, there are events that we will
log."  S1599.2.25 then declines to provide a debugger: "This functionality will not
implement a 'debug TACACS+' command as log messages are considered sufficient."  So on
this feature a missing log line is not a cosmetic gap.  It removes the only diagnostic
the design offers.  That is the standard this case grades against.

