CAVEAT:  What this run did NOT establish.
         1. S1599.1.084 and S1599.1.085, the log messages for "enable" authentication
            succeeding and failing, are NOT MEASURED.  They are two of the seven
            specifications this case exists to sweep.  Producing them needs
            "aaa authentication enable default group tacacs+ ...".  A Rejected enable
            then leaves the operator at awplus> with no way into configuration mode on
            any access path, because the console and every VTY share one enable method
            list.  The server holds no enable credential for these users, so a Reject
            is the likely outcome.  AW+ offers no recovery except a reload, and a
            reload was forbidden for this run, because the vlan10 path to the server
            exists in the running-config only.  So this case covers 5 of the 7 logging
            specifications.  The two it does not cover are named here, not glossed
            over.
         2. Reboot persistence is NOT MEASURED for this group.  No reload was
            performed.
         3. Not exercised: a malformed REPLY being discarded and logged (S1599.1.005,
            .006, .007), which needs a purpose-written server; whether the log buffer
            keeps these messages across a reboot; their behaviour through a configured
            remote syslog host; and the permanent log ("show log permanent").  Only the
            buffered log was read.

