  FINDING 1 -- S1599.1.080 is not implemented.  A successful first exchange with a
  TACACS+ server is logged nowhere.

  Two round trips to the server completed successfully and were recorded by the server
  itself.  The DUT produced no log message of any kind about establishing
  communication.  STEP 5 confirms this again, where a server that had gone Dead came
  back to Alive and again produced no message.
  The DUT does track the state.  "show tacacs+" carries a per-server Status column.
  But "show" is not the interface the TFS specifies, and a "show" cannot be sent to a
  syslog collector, which is the "help with debugging customer issues" purpose the
  Logging specifications section states.
  Severity: medium-low.  The absence is felt least when things are working.  But it
  also means there is no timestamped record of when a server came back, and that is
  exactly what a post-incident investigation asks for.  Against S1599.1.080, with TPS
  row 277 saying Supported: Yes.

  => STEP 3 PASS as a measurement: the step ran, the exchange is proven to have
     happened on the server side, and the DUT's log is proven to say nothing about it.
     The measurement is sound, and the result is FINDING 1.

