  12 packets captured
  FILEWIN /var/log/tac_plus.acct ... new-lines=1
  Oct 20 14:52:37 | manager | ttyS0 | unknown | stop | stop_time=1792461143 | task_id=60 ... elapsed_time=38

  tcpflow: 12 packet(s) total, 1 TCP flow(s)
    10.38.22.34:60842 -> 10.38.22.33:49  payload 165 B
    10.38.22.33:49 -> 10.38.22.34:60842  payload  17 B

  That one record is correct, and it is not a leak.  It is the STOP for the console
  session that had logged in WHILE accounting was still configured.  This is
  S1599.1.026 again: a session keeps the configuration it had at login, so its STOP is
  still sent after the configuration is removed.  The accounting file names it as a
  "stop" record with elapsed_time=38, which identifies it.

